</div>

<!-- ═══════════════ DKIM GUIDE ═══════════════ -->
<div id="ew-panel-dkim" role="tabpanel" style="display:none;">
  <p class="ew-intro">DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) adds a cryptographic signature to outgoing emails. Receiving servers verify the signature using a public key in your DNS. Most providers generate the keys for you -- you just publish the DNS record they give you.</p>

  <div class="ew-info-cards">
    <div class="ew-info-card">
      <strong>How DKIM works</strong>
      <ol class="ew-info-list">
        <li>Your mail server signs each outgoing message with a private key.</li>
        <li>The signature is added to the <code>DKIM-Signature</code> email header.</li>
        <li>The public key is published as a DNS TXT record at <code>selector._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code>.</li>
        <li>Receiving servers fetch the public key and verify the signature.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="ew-info-card">
      <strong>Key recommendations</strong>
      <ul class="ew-info-list" style="list-style:disc;">
        <li><strong>Minimum 2048-bit RSA keys</strong> -- 1024-bit is considered weak and some receivers reject it.</li>
        <li>Rotate keys at least annually.</li>
        <li>Use a unique selector per service (e.g., <code>google</code>, <code>sendgrid</code>).</li>
        <li>Consider Ed25519 where both your sender and receivers support it; keys and signatures are smaller than RSA, but provider support varies.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ew-section-label">Provider-specific DKIM setup</div>
  <div class="ew-dkim-providers">
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>Google Workspace</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Go to <strong>Google Admin Console</strong> &rarr; Apps &rarr; Google Workspace &rarr; Gmail &rarr; Authenticate email.</li>
        <li>Select your domain and click <strong>Generate New Record</strong>.</li>
        <li>Choose 2048-bit key length and a prefix (default: <code>google</code>).</li>
        <li>Copy the generated TXT record value.</li>
        <li>Add a TXT record at <code>google._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code> with the value.</li>
        <li>Return to Admin Console and click <strong>Start Authentication</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>Microsoft 365</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Go to <strong>Microsoft 365 Defender</strong> &rarr; Email &amp; collaboration &rarr; Policies &rarr; Threat policies &rarr; Email authentication settings.</li>
        <li>Select your domain under DKIM.</li>
        <li>Microsoft provides two CNAME records (selector1 and selector2).</li>
        <li>Add both CNAME records in your DNS:
          <br><code>selector1._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code> &rarr; <code>selector1-yourdomain-com._domainkey.yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com</code>
          <br><code>selector2._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code> &rarr; <code>selector2-yourdomain-com._domainkey.yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com</code>
        </li>
        <li>Toggle DKIM signing to <strong>Enabled</strong> after DNS propagation.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>SendGrid</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Go to <strong>SendGrid Dashboard</strong> &rarr; Settings &rarr; Sender Authentication &rarr; Authenticate Your Domain.</li>
        <li>Enter your domain and select your DNS host.</li>
        <li>SendGrid generates three CNAME records for you.</li>
        <li>Add all three CNAME records to your DNS.</li>
        <li>Return to SendGrid and click <strong>Verify</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>Amazon SES</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>In <strong>AWS SES Console</strong> &rarr; Verified identities &rarr; Your domain &rarr; Authentication tab.</li>
        <li>Under DKIM, click <strong>Generate DKIM tokens</strong> (Easy DKIM with 2048-bit keys).</li>
        <li>SES generates three CNAME records. Add them to your DNS.</li>
        <li>SES automatically verifies once DNS propagates (may take up to 72 hours).</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>Self-hosted (OpenDKIM)</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Install OpenDKIM: <code>apt install opendkim opendkim-tools</code></li>
        <li>Generate a key pair:
          <br><code>opendkim-genkey -s default -d yourdomain.com -b 2048</code></li>
        <li>This creates <code>default.private</code> (private key) and <code>default.txt</code> (DNS record).</li>
        <li>Add the contents of <code>default.txt</code> as a TXT record at <code>default._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code>.</li>
        <li>Configure OpenDKIM in <code>/etc/opendkim.conf</code> and integrate with your MTA (Postfix, Exim, etc.).</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="ew-section-label" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">DKIM record template</div>
  <div class="ew-form-grid">
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dkim-domain">Your domain</label>
      <input type="text" id="ew-dkim-domain" placeholder="example.com" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dkim-selector">Selector</label>
      <input type="text" id="ew-dkim-selector" placeholder="default" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
      <span class="ew-field-hint">Usually "default", "google", "s1", "selector1", or whatever your provider assigns</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group" style="grid-column:1/-1;">
      <label for="ew-dkim-pubkey">Public key (base64, without BEGIN/END headers)</label>
      <textarea id="ew-dkim-pubkey" rows="3" placeholder="MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQ..." spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" style="font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);font-size:0.8rem;"></textarea>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ew-result-block">
    <div class="ew-result-label">DNS TXT Record</div>
    <div class="ew-record-name" id="ew-dkim-record-name">default._domainkey.example.com</div>
    <div class="output-area" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
      <button class="btn btn--copy" id="ew-dkim-copy">Copy</button>
      <pre id="ew-dkim-output" style="white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-all;"></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════ DMARC POLICY ═══════════════ -->
<div id="ew-panel-dmarc" role="tabpanel" style="display:none;">
  <p class="ew-intro">DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance) tells receiving servers how to handle emails that fail SPF or DKIM checks. It also enables reporting so you can monitor who is sending email from your domain.</p>

  <div class="ew-form-grid">
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-domain">Your domain</label>
      <input type="text" id="ew-dmarc-domain" placeholder="example.com" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-policy">Policy (p=)</label>
      <select id="ew-dmarc-policy">
        <option value="none">none -- Monitor only, no action</option>
        <option value="quarantine">quarantine -- Send failures to spam</option>
        <option value="reject" selected>reject -- Block failing emails (recommended)</option>
      </select>
      <span class="ew-field-hint">Start with "none" to collect data, then ramp to quarantine and eventually reject.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-sp">Subdomain policy (sp=)</label>
      <select id="ew-dmarc-sp">
        <option value="">Inherit from main policy</option>
        <option value="none">none</option>
        <option value="quarantine">quarantine</option>
        <option value="reject">reject</option>
      </select>
      <span class="ew-field-hint">Override the policy for subdomains. Useful if you don't send email from subdomains.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-pct">Percentage (pct=)</label>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;">
        <input type="range" id="ew-dmarc-pct" min="1" max="100" value="100" style="flex:1;">
        <span id="ew-dmarc-pct-val" style="font-weight:700;font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);min-width:40px;text-align:right;color:var(--text-1,#e2e8f0);">100%</span>
      </div>
      <span class="ew-field-hint">Start at 10% during rollout. Ramp to 100% once you've verified legitimate mail passes.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-rua">Aggregate report email (rua=)</label>
      <input type="email" id="ew-dmarc-rua" placeholder="dmarc-reports@example.com" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
      <span class="ew-field-hint">Daily XML reports showing who sends email from your domain. Highly recommended.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-ruf">Forensic report email (ruf=)</label>
      <input type="email" id="ew-dmarc-ruf" placeholder="dmarc-forensic@example.com" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off">
      <span class="ew-field-hint">Individual failure reports. Many ISPs no longer send these due to privacy concerns.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-adkim">DKIM alignment (adkim=)</label>
      <select id="ew-dmarc-adkim">
        <option value="r">r -- Relaxed (subdomains pass)</option>
        <option value="s">s -- Strict (exact domain match required)</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-group">
      <label for="ew-dmarc-aspf">SPF alignment (aspf=)</label>
      <select id="ew-dmarc-aspf">
        <option value="r">r -- Relaxed (subdomains pass)</option>
        <option value="s">s -- Strict (exact domain match required)</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ew-result-block" style="margin-top:1rem;">
    <div class="ew-result-label">DNS TXT Record</div>
    <div class="ew-record-name" id="ew-dmarc-record-name">_dmarc.example.com</div>
    <div class="output-area" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
      <button class="btn btn--copy" id="ew-dmarc-copy">Copy</button>
      <pre id="ew-dmarc-output" style="white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-all;"></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="ew-dmarc-explain" class="ew-explain"></div>

  <div class="ew-rollout-guide">
    <div class="ew-rollout-title">Recommended rollout sequence</div>
    <div class="ew-rollout-steps">
      <div class="ew-rollout-step">
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-badge">Step 1</div>
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-body">
          <strong>p=none, pct=100</strong>
          <span>Monitor-only mode. No emails are blocked or filtered. Publish this record and collect aggregate reports for 2–4 weeks. Identify all legitimate sending sources in your rua= reports before enforcing anything.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ew-rollout-arrow">&#8595;</div>
      <div class="ew-rollout-step">
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-badge">Step 2</div>
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-body">
          <strong>p=quarantine, pct=10</strong>
          <span>Start enforcement at 10% of failing messages — these go to spam. Monitor reports for legitimate mail getting caught. If clean after a week, increase pct to 50, then 100.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ew-rollout-arrow">&#8595;</div>
      <div class="ew-rollout-step">
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-badge">Step 3</div>
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-body">
          <strong>p=quarantine, pct=100</strong>
          <span>All failing messages go to spam. Hold this position for 1–2 weeks to confirm no legitimate senders are misconfigured. Review rua= reports carefully.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ew-rollout-arrow">&#8595;</div>
      <div class="ew-rollout-step ew-rollout-step--final">
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-badge ew-rollout-step-badge--final">Step 4</div>
        <div class="ew-rollout-step-body">
          <strong>p=reject, pct=100</strong>
          <span>Requests reject handling for messages that fail aligned DMARC checks; receivers retain final policy. This can reduce direct-domain spoofing but does not stop look-alike domains, display-name abuse, or every phishing path. Keep monitoring rua= reports.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════ DEPLOY GUIDE ═══════════════ -->
<div id="ew-panel-deploy" role="tabpanel" style="display:none;">
  <p class="ew-intro">Once you have your records, add them as TXT records in your DNS provider. Here are step-by-step instructions for popular providers.</p>

  <div class="ew-deploy-providers">
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail" open>
      <summary>Cloudflare</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Log in to the <a href="https://dash.cloudflare.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ew-link">Cloudflare dashboard</a> and select your domain.</li>
        <li>Go to <strong>DNS</strong> &rarr; <strong>Records</strong> &rarr; <strong>Add record</strong>.</li>
        <li>Set Type to <strong>TXT</strong>.</li>
        <li>For SPF: set Name to <strong>@</strong> (root domain). For DMARC: set Name to <strong>_dmarc</strong>.</li>
        <li>Paste the generated record value into <strong>Content</strong>.</li>
        <li>Set TTL to <strong>Auto</strong> and click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
        <li>Proxy status does not apply to TXT records.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>AWS Route 53</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Open the <a href="https://console.aws.amazon.com/route53/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ew-link">Route 53 console</a> and select your hosted zone.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Create record</strong>.</li>
        <li>For SPF: leave Record name blank (root). For DMARC: enter <strong>_dmarc</strong>.</li>
        <li>Set Record type to <strong>TXT</strong>.</li>
        <li>In Value, paste the record wrapped in <strong>double quotes</strong>: <code>"v=spf1 ..."</code></li>
        <li>Set TTL to <strong>300</strong> (5 minutes is fine during testing).</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Create records</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>GoDaddy</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Log in to <a href="https://dcc.godaddy.com/domains" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ew-link">GoDaddy Domain Manager</a>.</li>
        <li>Select your domain &rarr; <strong>DNS</strong> tab &rarr; <strong>DNS Records</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Add New Record</strong>.</li>
        <li>Select Type: <strong>TXT</strong>.</li>
        <li>For SPF: set Host to <strong>@</strong>. For DMARC: set Host to <strong>_dmarc</strong>.</li>
        <li>Paste the record value into <strong>TXT Value</strong>.</li>
        <li>Set TTL to <strong>1 Hour</strong> and click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>Namecheap</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Log in to <a href="https://ap.www.namecheap.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ew-link">Namecheap</a> &rarr; Domain List &rarr; <strong>Manage</strong> your domain.</li>
        <li>Go to <strong>Advanced DNS</strong> tab.</li>
        <li>Under Host Records, click <strong>Add New Record</strong>.</li>
        <li>Select Type: <strong>TXT Record</strong>.</li>
        <li>For SPF: set Host to <strong>@</strong>. For DMARC: set Host to <strong>_dmarc</strong>.</li>
        <li>Paste the record value into <strong>Value</strong>.</li>
        <li>Set TTL to <strong>Automatic</strong> and click the green checkmark to save.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>Google Domains / Squarespace</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Google Domains migrated to Squarespace. Go to <a href="https://domains.squarespace.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ew-link">Squarespace Domains</a>.</li>
        <li>Select your domain &rarr; <strong>DNS</strong> &rarr; <strong>DNS Settings</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Add record</strong>.</li>
        <li>Type: <strong>TXT</strong>. Host: <strong>@</strong> (SPF) or <strong>_dmarc</strong> (DMARC).</li>
        <li>Paste the record value and save.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
    <details class="ew-dkim-detail">
      <summary>DigitalOcean</summary>
      <ol class="ew-steps">
        <li>Go to <a href="https://cloud.digitalocean.com/networking/domains" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ew-link">DigitalOcean Networking</a> &rarr; Domains.</li>
        <li>Select your domain.</li>
        <li>Under <strong>Create new record</strong>, select <strong>TXT</strong>.</li>
        <li>For SPF: set Hostname to <strong>@</strong>. For DMARC: set Hostname to <strong>_dmarc</strong>.</li>
        <li>Paste the value and set TTL to <strong>3600</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Create Record</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="ew-deploy-tip" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
    <strong>Verification tips</strong>
    <ul class="ew-deploy-tip-list">
      <li>DNS propagation can take 5 minutes to 48 hours. Most changes propagate within 15 minutes.</li>
      <li>Use <code>dig TXT yourdomain.com</code> or <code>nslookup -type=txt yourdomain.com</code> to verify.</li>
      <li>For DMARC: <code>dig TXT _dmarc.yourdomain.com</code></li>
      <li>For DKIM: <code>dig TXT selector._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code></li>
      <li>Send a test email to a Gmail address and check the original message headers for SPF, DKIM, and DMARC pass/fail.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

